From: jgrizon
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:18:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] shader: wave64 reduce covers first lanes on the wave-path
 assumption (off)

The reductions still refused after the strict uniform_control gate have their
reduction blocks behind lane branches, which uniform_control rejects. A lane
branch does not split the two host waves (both execute both sides, masked);
only a scalar branch can, and VICTORY_WAVE64_REDUCE already assumes both
halves compute the same scalars. barriers::wave_path therefore treats every
branch and jump edge as traversable and only an indirect exit as unsafe, and
the reduction gate and a first-lane read on the same path use it. A first-lane
read there uses first_lane_across (the halves' own first lanes exchanged
through threadgroup memory) instead of answering from the reader's half.

uniform_control stays as the strict form, test-only, so the two are told
apart.

Ported from paveledits/ScarlettMac runtime-preview/checkpoint/patches/0014-shader-wave64-reduce-covers-first-lanes-on-the-wave-.patch

